  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Read your denial letter and policy details right away to find the exact reason your insurer rejected the claim.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "Read your denial letter and policy details right away to find the exact reason your insurer rejected the claim"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Immediate Action Steps"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Protect the roof: Put a temporary tarp over the damaged area to stop further leaks, but do not start permanent repairs. Permanent fixes can destroy the evidence you need.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get an independent inspection: Hire an independent, licensed roofing contractor or a HAAG Certified Inspector\n\nto check the roof and document missed damage with clear photos.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "HAAG Certified Inspector",
                "link": "https://weathershieldroofers.com/blog/insurance-denied-roof-claim-what-to-do/"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Request a re-inspection: Ask your insurance company for a second review, and make sure your independent roofer is present to point out the damage to the new adjuster.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Gather weather data: Pull official weather reports for the date of the storm or hail event to prove severe weather hit your specific area."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          6
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Escalation Options"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "File a formal appeal: Submit a written dispute that includes your independent inspection report, photos with timestamps, and specific policy sections."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Invoke the appraisal clause: If you and the insurer disagree on the repair cost rather than the coverage itself, ask for a formal appraisal where independent appraisers and a neutral umpire decide the value."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Hire a public adjuster: Consider hiring a licensed public adjuster to negotiate directly with the insurance company on your behalf."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Contact state regulators: File a formal complaint with your state's department of insurance if you believe the company acted unfairly."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Consult an attorney: Speak with an insurance claims lawyer if the insurer acts in bad faith or refuses to pay a valid, large claim."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          8
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you can share the reason listed in your denial letter and the type of storm damage (hail, wind, or wear and tear), I can give you more specific advice for your next step."
      }
    ],
